    {
      "title": "try/catch/finally and Throwing Errors",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "try/catch/finally and Throwing Errors",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. try / catch / finally",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`try { risky() } catch (err) { handle(err) } finally { cleanup() }`",
                "==finally== runs on success, on throw, and even after `return`",
                "`catch { ... }` is the optional binding: no error object needed",
                "{red:return in finally} overrides the try/catch return and swallows a pending throw"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "function f() {",
                "  try { return 'try'; }",
                "  finally { console.log('cleanup'); }",
                "}",
                "console.log(f());"
              ],
              "note": "finally runs before the function returns"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "output",
              "lines": [
                "cleanup",
                "try"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Throwing and Rethrowing",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "throw new Error('msg')",
                "throw 'msg'"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Stack",
                  "{green:set at throw site}",
                  "{red:none}"
                ],
                [
                  "instanceof",
                  "works",
                  "{red:breaks}"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Rethrow what you cannot handle: `if (!(err instanceof ValidationError)) throw err`",
                "Never leave an empty `catch {}`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. What catch Can See",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "try { await fetch(url); } catch (e) { handle(e); }",
                "try { fetch(url); } catch (e) { handle(e); }"
              ],
              "note": "1st is caught; 2nd rejection escapes the catch"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "catch sees only ==synchronous throws== and ==awaited rejections==. No `await`, no catch."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Custom Errors and error.cause",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Custom Errors and error.cause",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Define a Custom Error",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`extends Error`, then call ==super(msg, opts)== **first**",
                "Set `this.name`, or it prints as plain `Error`",
                "Passing `opts` to super lets ==cause== flow through"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "class ValidationError extends Error {",
                "  constructor(msg, opts) {",
                "    super(msg, opts);",
                "    this.name = 'ValidationError';",
                "    this.field = 'email';",
                "  }",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "extra fields: this.field, this.status = 404"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Check type: `err instanceof ValidationError`",
                "{red:Never} match `err.message` strings",
                "Handlers branch on ==fields== like `err.status`, no parsing"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Wrap with error.cause",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "try { load(); } catch (err) {",
                "  throw new Error('Load failed', { cause: err });",
                "}",
                "// walk the chain",
                "while (e) { report(e); e = e.cause; }"
              ],
              "note": "the original error stays attached as err.cause"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Wrap lower-level failures, keep the **original** error",
                "DevTools and Node print the nested ==cause== under the main stack"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Forgot opts?",
              "text": "A constructor that calls `super(msg)` only **drops** the cause. Forward `opts`."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Unhandled Promise Rejections",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Unhandled Promise Rejections",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. When a Rejection Is Unhandled",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Rejected promise with no `.catch` and no `await` in try/catch = ==unhandled==",
                "Browser: `window.addEventListener('unhandledrejection', fn)`",
                "Node: `process.on('unhandledRejection', fn)`",
                "Node 15+ ==kills the process== by default; browsers only {orange:log} it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. How Errors Escape",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`async` function always returns a promise: a `throw` becomes a ==rejection==, never a sync throw",
                "Missing `await` or `return` ==detaches== the chain; outer try/catch misses it"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "javascript",
              "lines": [
                "async function save() {",
                "  try { fetch('/api'); }   // no await: escapes",
                "  catch (e) { /* never runs */ }",
                "  try { await fetch('/api'); }",
                "  catch (e) { report(e); }  // caught",
                "}"
              ],
              "note": "await keeps the rejection inside try"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Promise.all",
                "Promise.allSettled"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "On failure",
                  "rejects on {red:first}, ignores rest",
                  "never rejects"
                ],
                [
                  "Result",
                  "array of values",
                  "`{status, value|reason}` each"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Global Handler",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Safety net only",
              "text": "Use the global `unhandledrejection` handler for ==logging and reporting==, not as the normal error path. Handle errors at the call site."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
